#{[17592186060029 "If $v = ⟨4,-1⟩$, then what is the magnitude of $v$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."] [17592186060119 "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a + 3b$ and points the same direction."] [17592186060126 "Let $a = ⟨ - 12, 3⟩$. Find $\\mid a \\mid$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."] [17592186060127 "![](images/2c/2c1f9580f07d06af7ec900ee63c95872e06f459107e64cf1b5117d928efdab22.png)\n\nLet $A(-4, 1)$ and $B(3, 0)$. Find $\\mid AB^(→) \\mid$."] [17592186060128 "![](images/0d/0d92a4d7b9c59b0d6bc8ffec9926bcf189c9bbe808c5bed7a02d6ab09bcebcd0.png)\n\nLet $P(-2, 2)$ and $Q(3, 3)$. Find $\\mid PQ^(→) \\mid$."] [17592186060129 "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a$ and points the same direction."] [17592186073998 "Using the method of substitution, find the solution of\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-7a + 2b &=18 \\\\ -6a + 6b &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186088018 "![](images/33/330409f3fa32ee8701066cd3b434800a9cf3ed18639ae6f871494240d8237d7f.png)\n\nThe line segment $XY^(―)$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(2, 2)$ and $(-4, 2)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?"] [17592186088019 "![](images/b2/b28b10cb5d033e2559f7e54e0745285f554d0bfbffa8e14d7bb6c2ba077fced8.png)\n\nThe line segment $XY^(―)$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(6, 4)$ and $(-4, 2)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?"] [17592186096968 "![](images/a8/a89a9c2ff1cfd53a9d9e33c60591b482cbfa4044e313b2d2c031046bb21e5ce3.png)\n\nThe vector $a$ is depicted above. Which of the following diagrams shows the vectors $3a$ and $-a$?"] [17592186097030 "Given that $4a - 12b$ and $λ(a - 3b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$."] [17592186097031 "Given that $λ(-0.5a + 6b)$ and $a - 12b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$."] [17592186097032 "![](images/f5/f54e51921dfd2fb1b93bccec89553e174e2527866352626a5bf0846956b096bb.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the vector $a$. Which of the following diagrams shows the vector $-\\frac{1}{2}a$?"] [17592186097247 "If a curve $C$ is given by $y = 2e^{x}(x + 1)$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x = 0$."] [17592186097260 "If a curve $C$ is given by $y = 8x^{3}\\sin x$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x = \\frac{π}{2}$."] [17592186106040 "The closed, positively oriented curve $C$ is defined as $r(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ The outward-pointing unit normal vector on $C$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nn=\\frac{a(t)\\,i+b(t)\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $a(t).$"] [17592186106041 "The closed curve $C$ is defined as $r(t)=7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+24\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ The outward-pointing unit normal vector for $C$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nn=\\frac{a(t)\\,i+b(t)\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $b(t).$\n\n*Hint: Observe that $C$ is traversed clockwise.*"] [17592186106043 "The closed curve $C$ is defined as $r(t)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ The outward-pointing unit normal vector for $C$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nn=\\frac{a(t)\\,i+b(t)\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $a(t).$\n\n*Hint: Observe that $C$ is traversed clockwise.*"] [17592186106060 "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=2xy,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186106063 "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=-3xz,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=\\sqrt{2}x+\\sqrt{2}y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186106094 "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a = ⟨k, 1, 1⟩$, $b = ⟨5, 0, 4⟩$, and $c = ⟨6, 2, 5⟩$ are coplanar."] [17592186106095 "Find $t$ given that the vectors $p=⟨3,t,t⟩$, $q=⟨1,3,1⟩$, and $r=⟨1,1,3⟩$ are coplanar."] [17592186106309 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $x=⟨3,5,0⟩$, $y=⟨3,2,0⟩$ and $z=⟨3,4,5⟩.$"] [17592186106310 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a = ⟨ - 3, 0,-2⟩$, $b = ⟨1, 5,-3⟩$, and $c = ⟨2,-1, 4⟩$."] [17592186114970 "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t,$ where $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i-\\left(\\frac{1}{t-2}\\right)\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =(4t-1)\\,i+{e}^{3t}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186114973 "Find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t),$ given the following functions $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\sqrt{t}\\,i+{t}^{2}j \\\\ g(t) & =\\frac{1}{t}i+{e}^{t}j\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186115760 "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2t-8 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)={t}^{2}.$"] [17592186115762 "Find $(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =20t\\,i-2t\\,j+(2+5t)\\,k \\\\ g(t) & ={t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j+({t}^{2}+t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186115764 "Find $(f\\times g)^{′}(t)$ where\n\n$$\nf(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3{t}^{2} \\\\ t+4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,g(t)=\\begin{bmatri