{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$"] [17592186124956 "Evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]$ at $t=1$ given that\n$$\n\\displaystyle ∇f(x,y)=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+3y}\\,i+\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+3y}\\,j\n$$\nand\n$r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j.$"] [17592186124959 "If $f(x,y,z)=xy+yz+xz$ and $r(t)=t\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j+e\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$"] [17592186124960 "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+3xyz$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},t+1,-t⟩$ at the point $t=1.$"] [17592186124961 "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-y)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨2\\sqrt{t},4t⟩$ at the point $t=1.$"] [17592186124962 "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=2x+{y}^{2}$ at the point $(0,1)$ in the direction of the vector $v=5i+2j.$"] [17592186124964 "Consider the function $g(x, y) = \\frac{x^{2}}{y}$. What is the rate of change of $g(x, y)$ at the point $(2, 1)$ in the direction of the vector $v = ⟨ - 1, 3⟩$?"] [17592186125024 "Find $f(x, y, z)$ such that $∇f(x, y, z) = F(x, y, z)$, where $F(x, y, z) = 2xyi + (x^{2} + 2z)j + 2yk$."] [17592186125061 "Find $f(x, y)$ such that $∇f(x, y) = F(x, y)$, where $F(x, y) = \\cos xi + \\sin yj$."] [17592186125229 "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where $F(x,y,z)=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,j-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,k.$"] [17592186125246 "Evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]$ at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ given that $∇f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,j$ and $r(t)=\\frac{t}{2}\\,i+t\\,j.$"] [17592186125249 "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡xy$ and $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$"] [17592186125250 "If $f(x,y,z)=z(x+y)$ and $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+{e}^{t}\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$"] [17592186134087 "Which of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)={y}^{2}\\,i-{x}^{2}\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,1]?$"] [17592186134088 "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y,z)=yz\\,i+xz\\,j+xy\\,k$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+{t}^{3}\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1].$"] [17592186134089 "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{C}F \\cdot dr\n$$ given that $F(x, y, z) = xi + yj + zk$ and $C$ is the path $r(t) = \\cos ti + \\sin tj + 2\\sqrt{t}k$ for $t ∈ [0, π]$."] [17592186134090 "Which of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)=y\\,i-x\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,\\pi ]?$"] [17592186134091 "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$ given that  $F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\,i+2y\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+t\\,j$ for $t\\in [1,2].$"] [17592186134212 "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$ given that $F(x,y)={x}^{2}y\\,i+(x+1)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=3t\\,i+(2+t)\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,1].$"] [17592186134276 "Which of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{2}(x-y)$ and the curve $C$ is parametrized \n by $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}+t,\\,{t}^{2}-t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,\\sqrt{2}]?$"] [17592186134277 "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x, y) = 3x$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $$\n\\displaystyle r(t) = ⟨\\frac{4t^{3/2}}{3}, \\frac{t^{2}}{2} - t⟩\n$$ for $t ∈ [0, 1]$."] [17592186134338 "Evaluate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_(C)(x^{2} + y^{2})ds,\n$$ where $C$ is the curve parametrized by $r(t) = 3(\\cos t + t\\sin t)i + 3(\\sin t - t\\cos t)j$ for $0 \\le t \\le 2π$."] [17592186134367 "Use Green's theorem to evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr,\n$$ where $F(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,{x}^{2}-2y⟩$ and $C$ is the boundary of the square $0\\le x\\le \\pi ,0\\le y\\le \\pi ,$ traversed counterclockwise."] [17592186134375 "Consider the square $C$ in the plane with vertices $(-1,0),(2,0),(2,3)$ and $(-1,3),$ traversed counterclockwise, and the region $D$ bounded by $C.$ Express $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr,\n$$  where $F(x,y)=⟨3xy,{x}^{2}y⟩,$ as a repeated integral."] [17592186134511 "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{12x}{y-1}$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+(t+1)\\,j\\,$ for $t\\in [\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{6}].$"] [17592186134512 "Evaluate the line integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_(C)4yz\\cos xds,\n$$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t) = ti + \\sin tj + k$ for $0 < t < \\frac{π}{2}$."] [17592186134513 "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_(C)(x^{3} - y)ds,\n$$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t) = 2ti + (2 - t)j$ for $-1 \\le t \\le 2$?"] [17592186161896 "Consider the curves $C_1$ and $C_2,$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨\\frac{1}{9}{t}^{3},\\,t⟩, & 0\\le t\\le 3 \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨3{u}^{3},\\,3u⟩, & 0\\le u\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose $$\n\\displaystyle\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k\n$$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = 3k\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k\n$$"] [17592186162326 "Suppose $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{C_{1}}f(x, y)ds = 2\n$$ for some function $f(x, y)$, where $C_{1}$ is parametrized by $r_{1}(t) = ⟨t, t^{2}⟩$ for $0 \\le t \\le 1$.\n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n\n1. $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{-C_{1}}f(x, y)ds =-2\n$$\n2. $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{-C_{1}}f(x, y)ds = 2\n$$\n3. $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{C_{2}}f(x, y)ds = 4,\n$$ where $C_{2}$ is parametrized by $r_{2}(u) = ⟨2u, 4u^{2}⟩$ for $0 \\le u \\le \\frac{1}{2}$."] [17592186176191 "$f(t, z) = ⟨2\\cos t, _____, z⟩$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(t, z)$ above parametrizes the elliptic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $x^{2} + y^{2} = 4$. What is the second component of $f$?"] [17592186176192 "$f(t, y) = ⟨2\\cos t, y, _____⟩$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(t, y)$ above parametrizes the elliptic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $9x^{2} + 4z^{2} = 36$. What is the third component of $f$?"] [17592186176193 "$$\nf(x,z)=⟨x,\\,\\text{___},\\,z⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(x,z)$ above parametrizes the parabolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $y=4{x}^{2}.$ What is the second component of $f?$"] [17592186176194 "$f(x, y) = ⟨___, y, 9y^{2}⟩$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(x, z)$ above parametrizes the parabolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $9y^{2} = z$. What is the first component of $f$?"] [17592186176195 "$$\nf(t,z)=⟨3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\text{_____},\\,z⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(t,z)$ above parametrizes one sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=9$ for $x\\ge 3.$ What is the second component of $f?$"] [17592186176400 "$$\n\\displaystyle f(x, t) = ⟨x, _____, 2\\sec t⟩, t ∈ (-\\frac{π}{2}, \\frac{π}{2})\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(x, t)$ above parametrizes one sheet of the hyperbolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $3z^{2} - 4y^{2} = 12$ for $z \\ge 2$. What is the second component of $f$?"] [17592186180021 "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=y\\,i-x\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$"] [17592186180028 "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{5}{y}\\,i+\\frac{1}{x}\\,j$ along the ellipse $C$ with equation $25{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25$ oriented counterclockwise."] [17592186235431 "If a curve $C$ is defined by the equation $y=f(x)\\cdot h(x),$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\pi .$\n\nSlope $\\,=${{field-1}}"] [17592186235461 "Find the norm of the fundamental vector product for the surface $r(x,\\theta ),$ found in the previous step.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n$‖{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′}‖=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n{{field-1}}"] [17592186235479 "If a curve $C$ is defined by the equation $y=f(x)\\cdot h(x),$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\pi .$\n\nSlope $\\,=${{field-1}}"] [17592186235525 "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=\\text{div}\\,V$ at the point $(1,1)$ in the direction of the vector $v=-3\\,i+4\\,j.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \nThe required directional derivative is ${f}_{u}^{′}(1,1)=$\n\n                                    \n 